moon:
I should be joyful with the stream of joy
Sent through me. But the moon is in my face ...
I dare not,—though I guess the name he loves;

moods:
Of subtly-changing and surprising parts;
His moods are storms that frighten and make glad,
His eyes were made to capture women’s hearts.

moons:
"Our only hope, more dear than vital breath,
"Twelve moons revolv'd, becomes the prey of death;
"Delightful infant, nightly visions give

moon's:
In every living thing;
On the moon’s yellow wings I glide,
On the wild rose I swing;

moonbeams:
As they passed over; evermore
The pallid moonbeams shone before;
And the wind hushed, and nothing stirred;

mooin:
Den a-lookin' roun' to ax each othah w'y.
Don' you hyeah dem cows a-mooin'? Dat 's dey howdy to de spring;
Ain' dey lookin' most oncommon satisfied?

moorings:
The wondrous nearer drew;
Hands bustled at the moorings --
The crowd respectful grew.

moonlighted:
Where the Babe sucked; or, Lamia in her first
Moonlighted pallor, ere she shrunk and blinked,
And, shuddering, wriggled down to the unclean;
